# 7. AUTHENTICATION AND SESSION MANAGEMENT

## 7.1 Authentication provider

Supabase Auth is the authentication authority.

No authentication implementation exists yet (D-04); implement it as specified in §7.2–§7.6.

## 7.2 Authentication requirements

For protected API operations:

1. Read the authenticated session using the trusted server-side Supabase client.
2. Validate the session.
3. Resolve the authenticated user.
4. Confirm the user is eligible to perform the operation.
5. Apply the relevant authorization checks.
6. Continue only after validation succeeds.

Never trust a user ID supplied by the browser as proof of identity.

The server must derive the authenticated user identity from the verified session.

## 7.3 User identity

For user-owned operations:

- Determine the current user from the authenticated session.
- Never allow the client to impersonate another user by changing a request body.
- Use the database's actual primary key type.
- The relationship between `auth.users` and application profile records is defined in KEA-DBS-002 §4.1 (`profiles.id` → `auth.users.id`).

Identifiers are UUIDs (KEA-DBS-002 §2.3); do not assume otherwise.

## 7.4 Session expiration

When a session expires:

- Protected API requests must fail appropriately.
- The frontend must receive a consistent authentication error.
- The user should be redirected through the approved login flow.
- Safe navigation context should be preserved where possible.

## 7.5 Guest access — Guest Session Rule (D-03, decided 2026-11-20)

A guest is an unauthenticated visitor, identified by a server-issued guest-session
token stored in the browser. A guest is NOT an account.

A guest MAY: browse public discovery; view polls/results and game descriptions;
vote in polls; play the 3 games.

A guest may NOT: post, comment, react, join communities, report content, or create
any game record associated with an account. (Guest game sessions are tied to the
guest session only, never to an account.)

LIMITED TIME: a guest participation window lasts **60 minutes from the guest
session's first vote or game start**, and ends on browser close, whichever is first.
After expiry the guest must register / log in to vote or play again.

One vote per poll per guest session. Guest votes are counted. Guest game scores are
not saved to a profile and do not appear on leaderboards.

After registration, guest-session votes/scores do NOT transfer to the new account
(no merge in MVP).

Rate limits apply per guest session + IP (thresholds TBD in P1 config — do not invent).

Guests may NOT change/remove a vote (see D-11, §12.7).

Do not assume that every GET endpoint is public.

For each endpoint, explicitly define:

- Public access.
- Guest-session access (per this rule).
- Authenticated access.
- Restricted authenticated access.
- Administrative access.

Guest users must not be allowed to execute authenticated actions.

## 7.6 Account status

The API must enforce restrictions associated with:

- Active accounts.
- Suspended accounts.
- Restricted accounts.
- Deleted or deactivated accounts.
- Unverified accounts where verification is required.

The exact account-status values must match KEA-DBS-002 (active, restricted, suspended, pending_deletion, deleted) and the approved authorization model.

Age eligibility: the MVP audience is **16+** (D-02). Users aged 16–17 are included in the 16+ audience; there is no adult-only content in the MVP; Ghana Data Protection Act 2012 (Act 843) / DPC review is still required before public launch. Do not invent any parental-consent mechanism — it is a legal-review item (TBD, owner Dennis, before public launch).

