## 22.3 Error monitoring

Sentry is the approved monitoring baseline (KEA-SAD-001); set it up in P0 — no integration exists yet (D-04).

Capture:

- Unexpected server errors.
- Failed database operations.
- Realtime subscription failures where useful.
- Unexpected authorization failures.
- Important frontend/API integration failures.

Do not capture sensitive information in error payloads.

## 22.4 Metrics

Where available, monitor:

- Request volume.
- Error rate.
- Endpoint latency.
- Database query latency.
- Rate-limit activity.
- Realtime connection health.
- Realtime reconnect frequency.
- Failed background operations.

Performance targets and alert thresholds must be established from actual usage and operational requirements rather than invented. (TBD — owner Dennis; see README Open Decisions register, D-22.)

